From 60a8e048ca68987038ddd5a49070684bc1ce69b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:50:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Sample biplanar YCbCr video surfaces

macOS 14 and later play Setup Assistant's background video into biplanar
IOSurfaces and bind each whole surface as one texture in a private Metal
format. Reims had no bytes for them: 14's background was grey, 15's a
flat colour, and 27's ten-bit 4K video was refused.

The draw and compute paths now read both planes (8- or 16-bit samples)
from the surface's plane records and stage RGBA8, memoized per surface,
in the order each format samples in:

- 500 to 510 convert in the sampler; 14's compositor reads R'G'B'.
- 540 to 542 return Cr, Y and Cb; VideoToolbox's kernels on 15 and 27
  apply their own matrix.
- 543 is 27's ten-bit 4K hello video. Its kernel reads Y, Cb and Cr, but
  handed that the Golden Gate Bridge comes out blue against Apple's own
  still of the scene; handed Y, Cr and Cb it matches. Why is not found.

The rest of the private range is refused rather than guessed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
